<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pedro de Peralta</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1584–<a href="/years/1666">1666</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pedro de Peralta was a Spanish colonial official who served as governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-mexico">New Mexico</a> from 1610 to 1614. On royal orders he moved the capital of the colony from San Gabriel to a new site and founded the town of Santa Fe around 1610. His quarrels with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/franciscans">Franciscans</a> over authority and Indian labour led to his arrest and imprisonment by the friars before he was cleared by the authorities in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico-city">Mexico City</a>.</p></div>
